  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA value remains network-concentrated:</strong> the top chains continue to capture the majority of distributed issuance and often set near-term market direction. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/newsletters/the-daily/2026-11-19-binance-gets-6-5-billion-freezing-order-cryptoquant-says-bitcoin-is-in-a-value-zone-and-more-443511\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Binance gets $6.5 billion freezing order, CryptoQuant says bitcoin is in a \u2018value zone\u2019, and more</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Institutional expansion is likely staged:</strong> large-scale adoption typically lands on proven networks first, then broadens as compliance, interoperability, and liquidity deepen. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/11/20/here-s-what-s-crashing-gold-and-likely-weighing-on-bitcoin-too\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Here&#x27;s what&#x27;s crashing gold and likely weighing on bitcoin too</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Custody and issuance integrations are moving rankings first:</strong> Chains that win custody and issuance integrations usually pull distributed value share before the broader RWA market total catches up. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/moonpay-seeks-us-bank-charter-for-stablecoin-custody-services?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MoonPay seeks US bank charter for stablecoin, custody services</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
